  "text": "Quick Start Main Page\n​\nIntroduction\nThis channel is intended as a guide for newer and returning players looking to jumpstart their way into RS3 PvM and Bossing. This page links to a host of pages, each dedicated to cover important subjects that help you on your PvM journey.\n⬥ General tips like setting up your game interface and basic money making to get started.\n⬥ New to PvM to get you to level 70 in every combat style! There are:\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Example upgrade orders and ability bars\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Guides on the important non-combat skills for PvM and some training methods\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Important quests to work towards\n⬥ New to Bossing assumes you already have most of the PvM knowledge and skill from New to PvM, and helps you set progression goals for bossing. This includes prayer flicking, good bosses for learning, how to learn PvM, and how to transition to full manual combat.\n⬥ Note that the discord links in here will refer to either of two Runescape Discord servers. If you have not joined these, the links won't work.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• The official Runescape Discord invite link\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• The PvM Encyclopedia invite link\nGeneral Tips\nBefore you begin, it can be helpful to get a few things out of the way:\n⬥ Setting up a good interface - see #interface-guide.\n​\nHelp and Guidance\nIf you ever feel stuck, confused, in need of teamforming, or wanting personal input on your PvM situation; there are several resources you can jump to.\n⬥ Joining a Clan (RS discord recruitment page: #RuneScape -> looking-for-group) or dedicated discord servers (PvMe Discord affiliates: #affiliates) can be great for getting (PvM) help or finding people to PvM with.\n⬥ You can ask Mentors in the RS Discord server for help #affiliates or look for groups in #RuneScape -> recruitment-all\n⬥ You can ask for advice in the pvm-help channel of the PvMe Discord server for all your PvM inquiries! #pvm-help\n​\nSkilling Goals\n⬥ There are many Skills in Runescape that are not direct combat skills, but that greatly impact your combat prowess through prayers, potions, perks, familiars, and relics. We covered these in #noncombat-skilling-guide. This page is relevant for New to PvM as well as New to Bossing readers.\n​\nEarly Money making \nTraining buyable skills and upgrading your gear can be expensive, but there are money making methods that are effective even as a lower-level player. These are just a few methods you can try out - there are a lot more methods in the game for you to explore.\n#early-moneymaking-ideas\n​\nNew to PvM\nThis covers helpful beginner PvM goals, quests, but also combat upgrade suggestions and ability bars to get you from level 1 to level 70.\n⬥ The go-to page that outlines early-game quests, good monsters for training, handy items and more: #early-game-combat\n⬥ Early  upgrade order & ability bar:#unknown-channel\n⬥ Early  upgrade order & ability bar: #unknown-channel\n⬥ Early  upgrade order & ability bar: #unknown-channel\n⬥ Early  upgrade order & ability bar:#unknown-channel\n​\nNew to Bossing\nThis covers important level 70+ combat-related goals and upgrading information. You don't have to read all of this right away, there is a lot, just know it exists for when you feel you need a hand.\n⬥ The go-to page that outlines mid to end-game quests, suggested monsters for training, handy items and more: #mid-game-combat\n⬥ The PvMe upgrade order for every style level 70-99: #upgrade-order\n⬥ High level ability bars for Revo, Revo++ and Revo++ (AoE): #revolution-bars\n⬥ A recommended order of bosses that teach you valuable PvM lessons: #bossing-path\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• One such PvM lesson is prayer flicking: #prayer-flicking\n⬥ Consumable items relevant to PvM and bossing: #consumables\n⬥ Permanent unlocks (abilities, spells, quest rewards): #permanent-unlocks\n⬥ Armour, weapons and their uses: #armour-and-weapons\n⬥ Damage per minute (DPM) basics: how to think about your ability rotation to deal more damage: #dpm-advice\n​\nBasic boss guides\nThe PvMe Discord has basic guides for almost every boss in Runescape.\n⬥ These guides have beginner preset recommendations (think level 70+ / stage 1 upgrade order), an overview of how the boss's mechanics work, and suggestions for how to deal with them: #unknown-channel\n​\n      \n    ",
  "normalizedText": "Quick Start Main Page ​ Introduction This channel is intended as a guide for newer and returning players looking to jumpstart their way into RS3 PvM and Bossing. This page links to a host of pages, each dedicated to cover important subjects that help you on your PvM journey. ⬥ General tips like setting up your game interface and basic money making to get started. ⬥ New to PvM to get you to level 70 in every combat style! There are: ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Example upgrade orders and ability bars ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Guides on the important non-combat skills for PvM and some training methods ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Important quests to work towards ⬥ New to Bossing assumes you already have most of the PvM knowledge and skill from New to PvM, and helps you set progression goals for bossing. This includes prayer flicking, good bosses for learning, how to learn PvM, and how to transition to full manual combat. ⬥ Note that the discord links in here will refer to either of two Runescape Discord servers. If you have not joined these, the links won't work. ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• The official Runescape Discord invite link ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• The PvM Encyclopedia invite link General Tips Before you begin, it can be helpful to get a few things out of the way: ⬥ Setting up a good interface - see #interface-guide. ​ Help and Guidance If you ever feel stuck, confused, in need of teamforming, or wanting personal input on your PvM situation; there are several resources you can jump to. ⬥ Joining a Clan (RS discord recruitment page: #RuneScape -> looking-for-group) or dedicated discord servers (PvMe Discord affiliates: #affiliates) can be great for getting (PvM) help or finding people to PvM with. ⬥ You can ask Mentors in the RS Discord server for help #affiliates or look for groups in #RuneScape -> recruitment-all ⬥ You can ask for advice in the pvm-help channel of the PvMe Discord server for all your PvM inquiries! #pvm-help ​ Skilling Goals ⬥ There are many Skills in Runescape that are not direct combat skills, but that greatly impact your combat prowess through prayers, potions, perks, familiars, and relics. We covered these in #noncombat-skilling-guide. This page is relevant for New to PvM as well as New to Bossing readers. ​ Early Money making Training buyable skills and upgrading your gear can be expensive, but there are money making methods that are effective even as a lower-level player. These are just a few methods you can try out - there are a lot more methods in the game for you to explore. #early-moneymaking-ideas ​ New to PvM This covers helpful beginner PvM goals, quests, but also combat upgrade suggestions and ability bars to get you from level 1 to level 70. ⬥ The go-to page that outlines early-game quests, good monsters for training, handy items and more: #early-game-combat ⬥ Early upgrade order & ability bar:#unknown-channel ⬥ Early upgrade order & ability bar: #unknown-channel ⬥ Early upgrade order & ability bar: #unknown-channel ⬥ Early upgrade order & ability bar:#unknown-channel ​ New to Bossing This covers important level 70+ combat-related goals and upgrading information. You don't have to read all of this right away, there is a lot, just know it exists for when you feel you need a hand. ⬥ The go-to page that outlines mid to end-game quests, suggested monsters for training, handy items and more: #mid-game-combat ⬥ The PvMe upgrade order for every style level 70-99: #upgrade-order ⬥ High level ability bars for Revo, Revo++ and Revo++ (AoE): #revolution-bars ⬥ A recommended order of bosses that teach you valuable PvM lessons: #bossing-path ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• One such PvM lesson is prayer flicking: #prayer-flicking ⬥ Consumable items relevant to PvM and bossing: #consumables ⬥ Permanent unlocks (abilities, spells, quest rewards): #permanent-unlocks ⬥ Armour, weapons and their uses: #armour-and-weapons ⬥ Damage per minute (DPM) basics: how to think about your ability rotation to deal more damage: #dpm-advice ​ Basic boss guides The PvMe Discord has basic guides for almost every boss in Runescape. ⬥ These guides have beginner preset recommendations (think level 70+ / stage 1 upgrade order), an overview of how the boss's mechanics work, and suggestions for how to deal with them: #unknown-channel ​",
